# Source: L08.md (A2.1 Conversatioun, Lektioun 8: invitations, estate agents,
# and household chores). New vocabulary was checked against LOD; the source's
# non-lemma compounds and plural-only terms are retained where appropriate.
# The handout gives both d'Chargen and d'Chargë; this lesson consistently uses
# d'Chargen. A1 vocabulary is reinforced through sentences, not re-taught as words.
# Grammar focus: subordinate conjunctions (well, datt, obwuel, wann) send the
# conjugated verb to the end; demonstratives agree with noun gender and number.

@lesson A2.10 "Housing & Housework"

# --- Housing and estate agents ---
@word de Haushalt = the household
@word d'Immobilie = the property
@word d'Chargen = the running costs
@word d'Gäschtentoilette = the guest toilet
@word d'Residence = the apartment block
@word d'Agence Immobilière = the estate agency
@word op Wunnengssich sinn = to be looking for a place to live

# --- Household chores ---
@word de Botzplang = the cleaning schedule
@word d'Botzgeschier = the cleaning equipment
@word de Staubsauger = the vacuum cleaner
@word d'Streckbriet = the ironing board
@word d'Streckeisen = the iron
@word de Stot = the housework

@sentence
@lu Ech sinn op Wunnengssich.
@en I am looking for a place to live.
@distractor-en working
@distractor-en visiting
@distractor-lu schaffen
@distractor-lu besichen

@sentence
@lu Hues du déi Annonce gelies?
@en Have you read that advertisement?
@distractor-en letter
@distractor-en price
@distractor-lu Bréif
@distractor-lu Präis

@sentence
@lu D'Appartement ass zu Iechternach.
@en The apartment is in Echternach.
@distractor-en Luxembourg
@distractor-en city
@distractor-lu Lëtzebuerg
@distractor-lu Stad

@sentence
@lu Op wéi engem Stack läit d'Appartement?
@en On which floor is the apartment?
@distractor-en price
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu Präis
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Et ass um Rez-de-chaussée.
@en It is on the ground floor.
@distractor-en attic
@distractor-en cellar
@distractor-lu Späicher
@distractor-lu Keller

@sentence
@lu Wéi vill kascht d'Appartement?
@en How much does the apartment cost?
@distractor-en where
@distractor-en rent
@distractor-lu Wou
@distractor-lu Loyer

@sentence
@lu Ass de Loyer mat oder ouni Chargen?
@en Is the rent with or without running costs?
@distractor-en price
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu Präis
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu D'Kichen ass voll equipéiert.
@en The kitchen is fully equipped.
@distractor-en separate
@distractor-en quiet
@distractor-lu separat
@distractor-lu roueg

@sentence
@lu Et gëtt e Keller an eng Parkplaz.
@en There is a cellar and a parking space.
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-en price
@distractor-lu Gaart
@distractor-lu Präis

@sentence
@lu Hausdéieren si leider verbueden.
@en Pets are unfortunately forbidden.
@distractor-en welcome
@distractor-en cheap
@distractor-lu erlaabt
@distractor-lu gënschteg

@sentence
@lu Mir plënneren an eng méi grouss Wunneng.
@en We are moving into a bigger apartment.
@distractor-en stay
@distractor-en smaller
@distractor-lu bleiwen
@distractor-lu kleng

@sentence
@lu Mir brauchen op d'mannst dräi Schlofzëmmeren.
@en We need at least three bedrooms.
@distractor-en two
@distractor-en kitchen
@distractor-lu zwee
@distractor-lu Kichen

@sentence
@lu D'Gäschtentoilette ass separat.
@en The guest toilet is separate.
@distractor-en underground
@distractor-en expensive
@distractor-lu ënnerierdesch
@distractor-lu deier

@sentence
@lu D'Residence huet eng ënnerierdesch Parkplaz.
@en The apartment block has an underground parking space.
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-en key
@distractor-lu Gaart
@distractor-lu Schlëssel

# --- Demonstratives: noun gender and number choose the form ---

@sentence
@lu Dës Wunneng ass ganz roueg.
@en This apartment is very quiet.
@distractor-en that
@distractor-en expensive
@distractor-lu Déi
@distractor-lu deier

@sentence
@lu Déi Wunneng huet kee Gaart.
@en That apartment has no garden.
@distractor-en this
@distractor-en cellar
@distractor-lu Dës
@distractor-lu Keller

@sentence
@lu Dëse Präis ass ze héich.
@en This price is too high.
@distractor-en those
@distractor-en low
@distractor-lu Déi
@distractor-lu niddreg

@sentence
@lu Dee Staubsauger ass schrecklech haart.
@en That vacuum cleaner is terribly loud.
@distractor-en this
@distractor-en quiet
@distractor-lu Dëse
@distractor-lu roueg

@sentence
@lu Dëst Appartement huet zwee Schlofzëmmeren.
@en This apartment has two bedrooms.
@distractor-en that
@distractor-en kitchen
@distractor-lu Dat
@distractor-lu Kichen

@sentence
@lu Dat Haus huet eng Terrass.
@en That house has a terrace.
@distractor-en this
@distractor-en cellar
@distractor-lu Dëst
@distractor-lu Keller

@sentence
@lu Dës Kichen ass fonkelnei.
@en This kitchen is brand new.
@distractor-en that
@distractor-en old
@distractor-lu Déi
@distractor-lu al

@sentence
@lu Déi Agence Immobilière huet gutt Offeren.
@en That estate agency has good offers.
@distractor-en this
@distractor-en prices
@distractor-lu Dës
@distractor-lu Präisser

# --- Main and dependent clauses: the finite verb closes the dependent clause ---

@sentence
@lu Meng Wunneng ass perfekt, well se grouss ass.
@en My apartment is perfect because it is large.
@distractor-en small
@distractor-en house
@distractor-lu kleng
@distractor-lu Haus

@sentence
@lu D'Chargen sinn niddreg, well d'Haus energieeffizient ass.
@en The running costs are low because the house is energy efficient.
@distractor-en high
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu héich
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu An der Annonce steet, datt et eng Parkplaz gëtt.
@en The advertisement says that there is a parking space.
@distractor-en cellar
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu Keller
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Ech maachen de Stot, obwuel et langweileg ass.
@en I do the housework although it is boring.
@distractor-en exciting
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu spannend
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Mir musse plënneren, wann eise Propriétär d'Haus verkeeft.
@en We have to move if our landlord sells the house.
@distractor-en buys
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu keeft
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Wann ech Zäit hunn, maachen ech d'Wäsch.
@en When I have time, I do the laundry.
@distractor-en dishes
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu Spull
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Obwuel d'Kichen kleng ass, ass si hell.
@en Although the kitchen is small, it is bright.
@distractor-en dark
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu donkel
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Well d'Appartement roueg ass, interesséiert et mech.
@en Because the apartment is quiet, I am interested in it.
@distractor-en noisy
@distractor-en garden
@distractor-lu haart
@distractor-lu Gaart

@sentence
@lu Ech weess, datt de Keller dréchen ass.
@en I know that the cellar is dry.
@distractor-en wet
@distractor-en attic
@distractor-lu naass
@distractor-lu Späicher

@sentence
@lu Wann d'Wäschmaschinn futti ass, wäsche mir bei menger Mamm.
@en When the washing machine is broken, we wash at my mother's place.
@distractor-en father
@distractor-en dry
@distractor-lu Papp
@distractor-lu dréchen

